With this amendment, dev-intent capture lands as the user-visible
handhold for the two-modes-and-multi-workspace programme: the
user's natural-language statement of "I'm here to develop pos-v2"
or "I'm here to use pos-v2" is captured once at first-run and
structurally honoured thereafter. Sibling sub-plans B (mode-
loading), E (classify_workspace replacement), and F (auto-load
partition) inherit a satisfied dev-intent precondition; their
dispatches are cleared.
